WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.770
…can we do more on the economy though?

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:12.710
Modi's biggest achievement in the last two years
has been the real uptick in a foreign direct

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:18.920
investment coming into India. India has, for
the first time, overtaken China in terms of

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:24.360
greenfield direct investment. This is essentially
people investing in new factories and new

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.329
projects in India.

00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:30.880
The biggest disappointment is among those
who thought that Modi would put in place deep

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.480
structural reforms. We're talking about things
like reforming India's labor laws. We're talking

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.980
about reforming the way land is acquired for
industry and infrastructure.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.920
We're talking about privatization of loss-making
companies. And in all of these cases, Modi

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:51.050
has either moved too slowly, or he's been
stymied in the upper house of parliament,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.670
or he's kicked these reforms to the state.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:59.420
The biggest challenge he faces is the creation
of jobs. He's going to be up for reelection

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:06.100
in 2019, and India needs to create 12 million
new jobs a year just to stay standing still

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.040
in place.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.270
How would you rate Modi's economic performance
over the last two years? Let us know your

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.330
thoughts in the comments below, and also let
us know if there any other topics that you

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.960
would like AEI scholars to look at in 60 seconds.

